2026-10-14 — Resolve Galley Reviewer forms from the published workflow design

Root causes: an existing defect could resolve its original `DEFECT_REPORT` again from the defect detail view, so the UI showed the Galley report form after case creation. The Reviewer Decision was a hardcoded workflow panel and was not represented as a supported, published Form Master purpose. Its historical-report renderer also treated a missing legacy submission row as a reason to show no review content. Consequently, the Reviewer decision was not resolved/rendered from an exact published operational form version.

Implementation: existing-case resolution now excludes the initial report form except for an eligible returned Galley correction. Galley cases in `REPORTED` or `UNDER_REVIEW` resolve only published `REVIEW_DECISION` versions at the matching stage; returned cases wait for correction. Form Master supports the purpose and its three approved workflow bindings. Publication validates exactly Decision, Assign Team and Remark with the required approved types/sources. The Reviewer screen fetches the case-scoped operational-form list, renders its configured labels/order and backend-sourced decision choices, loads eligible teams through the existing authorized decision-options API, and submits the selected published `formId` and `versionId` to the existing reviewer-decision endpoint. A missing versioned Auditor submission no longer blocks a Reviewer decision; the typed defect details remain available. The server validates the Galley area, review status, current published form/version, routed Reviewer scope, team tenant/active/eligibility constraints, and decision atomically. Decisions continue to use append-only defect events; Reviewer decisions are not stored as generic operational submissions. V32 only adds the supported purpose/stage constraint and leaves submission purposes unchanged.

